[{:db/id "q-342630/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "331946e1-ff14-5810-9cfc-9f1687ca1f2b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342630/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "25e736c3-94dc-5701-b9f3-7197af2f78b0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-342630/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-342630/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342630" :question/id #uuid "6c621db2-dac4-5875-9a39-cffdb06bb23a" :question/math-academy-id "q-342630" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={({x}^{2}+2x+1)}^{2},$ the slope at the point $(0,1)$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the slope at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nWe use the chain rule to find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\nFirst, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf={g}^{2},\\,g={x}^{2}+2x+1\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=2g,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=2x+2.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =2g\\cdot (2x+2) \\\\  & =2({x}^{2}+2x+1)(2x+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line at the point where $x=0$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=0} & =[2({x}^{2}+2x+1)(2x+2){]}_{x=0} \\\\  & =2((0{)}^{2}+2\\cdot (0)+1)(2\\cdot (0)+2) \\\\  & =2(1)(2) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-342630/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "29956ecb-a28a-5406-b8dc-9776e9a3ccee"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342630"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-342663/field-1/1c35128c59a7847a115977df43414655602222d4153c898daa47f08b0f9b4500" :answer/id #uuid "aee374a3-f35d-5a18-9168-bbd221cd532b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-96" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342663/field-1/bc787d823ec953ec5e44b8f7f4a4c7f3b5de4a6a5f1cea9c5a660d6b5e6faac7" :answer/id #uuid "e9d6eb93-abe6-506e-9f4d-27d032f5b307" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "96" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342663/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6e0a6ce5-d38e-5ba3-9859-5d1d4c8be904" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-342663/field-1/1c35128c59a7847a115977df43414655602222d4153c898daa47f08b0f9b4500" :answer-field/choices ["q-342663/field-1/1c35128c59a7847a115977df43414655602222d4153c898daa47f08b0f9b4500" "q-342663/field-1/bc787d823ec953ec5e44b8f7f4a4c7f3b5de4a6a5f1cea9c5a660d6b5e6faac7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342663" :question/id #uuid "b8f5684d-fcfe-57b2-9c61-e436cca4178c" :question/math-academy-id "q-342663" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={(3x+1)}^{4},$ the slope at the point $(-1,16)$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the slope at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nWe use chain rule to find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\nFirst, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf={g}^{4},\\,g=3x+1\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=4{g}^{3},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=3.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =4{g}^{3}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =12(3x+1{)}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line at the point where $x=-1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=-1} & =[12(3x+1{)}^{3}{]}_{x=-1} \\\\  & =12(3\\cdot (-1)+1{)}^{3} \\\\  & =12(-2{)}^{3} \\\\  & =-96.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-342663/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "29956ecb-a28a-5406-b8dc-9776e9a3ccee"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342663"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-342910/field-1/9c89a40784b29c4193574944c3721c8d01b340894730f5261e7b22a2e75bcf57" :answer/id #uuid "4009a7a8-f560-5d9d-85b4-69dc9ec95449" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6x+11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342910/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "810de85e-ab03-5b53-8538-bb4a0f108607" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-342910/field-1/9c89a40784b29c4193574944c3721c8d01b340894730f5261e7b22a2e75bcf57" :answer-field/choices ["q-342910/field-1/9c89a40784b29c4193574944c3721c8d01b340894730f5261e7b22a2e75bcf57"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342910" :question/id #uuid "8d4112c3-c428-58ac-aa36-5e59e60a5e82" :question/math-academy-id "q-342910" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=(3-2x{)}^{3},$ the equation of the tangent at the point $(2,-1)$ is\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the slope at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nWe use the chain rule to find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\nFirst, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf={g}^{3},\\,g=3-2x\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=3{g}^{2},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=-2.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =3{g}^{2}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-6(3-2x{)}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line at the point where $x=2$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=2} & =(-6{(3-2x)}^{2}){|}_{x=2} \\\\  & =-6{(3-2(2))}^{2} \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the slope of the tangent line at the point $(2,-1)$ is $m=-6.$ Now, we find the equation of the tangent at that point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y+1 & =-6\\cdot (x-2) \\\\ y & =-6x+12-1 \\\\ y & =-6x+11\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-342910/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "29956ecb-a28a-5406-b8dc-9776e9a3ccee"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342910"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11410/selection/b7f958adf28f3b540f597d08269bbb9cf14eb5a1aca4061ee8566180ff832c14" :answer/id #uuid "4a8f7e36-1dc3-5309-a62b-70d51a7a99f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6{(5x+10)}^{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11410/selection/ce9ed90d4cbe08f334309ae972a37c81c72b3ff2ab2ebbb14e148a140235113b" :answer/id #uuid "592db5fa-308d-51ae-8dad-09a44868c0ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30{(5x+10)}^{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11410/selection/0fcbd0fdd1e3a16dbc166c1cde2284e2bf4b593eda955874cc0b6c2539997489" :answer/id #uuid "dde46f62-0e8a-5937-8599-447986204348" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30{(5x+10)}^{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11410/selection/821c03b7af36bef1771325f91f7ea418e469519a02c211c805edd6cb97acd7b2" :answer/id #uuid "c1fd9c23-4b19-53fa-9aeb-7fc689ebf7f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10{(5x+10)}^{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11410/selection/78731ec64a230be2879e6aa3f20d9d779d53439f8ec4cea607c80b477fbc9086" :answer/id #uuid "dca110dc-5ab7-5744-b84c-2257e5ed49f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5{(5x+10)}^{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11410/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f854dc8c-7fd9-57d7-8b3b-7fc5bbf2526b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11410/selection/0fcbd0fdd1e3a16dbc166c1cde2284e2bf4b593eda955874cc0b6c2539997489" :answer-field/choices ["q-11410/selection/b7f958adf28f3b540f597d08269bbb9cf14eb5a1aca4061ee8566180ff832c14" "q-11410/selection/ce9ed90d4cbe08f334309ae972a37c81c72b3ff2ab2ebbb14e148a140235113b" "q-11410/selection/0fcbd0fdd1e3a16dbc166c1cde2284e2bf4b593eda955874cc0b6c2539997489" "q-11410/selection/821c03b7af36bef1771325f91f7ea418e469519a02c211c805edd6cb97acd7b2" "q-11410/selection/78731ec64a230be2879e6aa3f20d9d779d53439f8ec4cea607c80b477fbc9086"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11410" :question/id #uuid "a2593795-1dac-5179-a216-eae1eb3b01c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-11410" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}$ when $f(x)={(5x+10)}^{6}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf={g}^{6},\\,g=5x+10\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=6{g}^{5},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=5.\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =6{g}^{5}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =30(5x+10{)}^{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-11410/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "29956ecb-a28a-5406-b8dc-9776e9a3ccee"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11410"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-342802/field-1/a32a0f7e64ab5ec8f15b0f308e5fdf0a8e3a7cac0bfab30d64cde5f86a67acae" :answer/id #uuid "2bdc1950-359f-5541-b420-602c2a526809" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{18}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342802/field-1/830a08a17a3bc68a8e849c8d7e7a7e21cd8b84724f1767acc4bccbeebb91b0c8" :answer/id #uuid "e72d69d4-a8d1-5761-8459-d98d546bccdd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{18}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342802/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "cfae2bb8-1a73-532a-855c-add69030b974" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-342802/field-1/a32a0f7e64ab5ec8f15b0f308e5fdf0a8e3a7cac0bfab30d64cde5f86a67acae" :answer-field/choices ["q-342802/field-1/a32a0f7e64ab5ec8f15b0f308e5fdf0a8e3a7cac0bfab30d64cde5f86a67acae" "q-342802/field-1/830a08a17a3bc68a8e849c8d7e7a7e21cd8b84724f1767acc4bccbeebb91b0c8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342802" :question/id #uuid "8e4c4d02-93ce-585f-897c-bbbbeb8472bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-342802" :question/is-example false :question/problem "The slope of the tangent to the curve $y=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3{x}^{2}+12x}}$ at the point where $x=2$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the slope at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nWe use the chain rule in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=3{x}^{2}+12x.$ Then $y=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}={u}^{-1/2}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=-\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{-3/2}=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=6x+12.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}}\\cdot (6x+12) \\\\  & =-\\frac{6x+12}{2\\sqrt{(3{x}^{2}+12x{)}^{3}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $x=2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=2} & ={(-\\frac{6x+12}{2\\sqrt{(3{x}^{2}+12x{)}^{3}}})|}_{x=2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{6(2)+12}{2\\sqrt{(3(2{)}^{2}+12(2){)}^{3}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{24}{2\\sqrt{{36}^{3}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{18}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-342802/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f0cdac9-57b2-5634-8d98-d6adf8a85204"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342802"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-314194/field-1/9228a9581d74ea4fcc74876545e8404172573b46c1a7d74c18b047af212805b1" :answer/id #uuid "fa95c1d6-3469-51b6-ac2b-ba7ab164518b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(2x+7)^3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-314194/field-1/67fb6f4a8e81e64ce7e496e0225ab7d097d0995a00fbcf652ca5800626ec2972" :answer/id #uuid "c76e134d-97f0-52ae-81e0-08ec088bdec9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(2x+7)^3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-314194/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "5d72aba1-a4a8-5bcd-9a5c-71653263fc1c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-314194/field-1/9228a9581d74ea4fcc74876545e8404172573b46c1a7d74c18b047af212805b1" :answer-field/choices ["q-314194/field-1/9228a9581d74ea4fcc74876545e8404172573b46c1a7d74c18b047af212805b1" "q-314194/field-1/67fb6f4a8e81e64ce7e496e0225ab7d097d0995a00fbcf652ca5800626ec2972"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-314194" :question/id #uuid "01d86967-f170-52eb-884c-faade3aec8eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-314194" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2x+7}}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the chain rule in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=2x+7.$ Then $y=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}={u}^{-1/2}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=-\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{-3/2}=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(2x+7{)}^{3}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-314194/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f0cdac9-57b2-5634-8d98-d6adf8a85204"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-314194"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-107291/selection/cbb27d87a8b1de240c6b24732b401bf8e15985669071cdb55cd79c7fc399a99f" :answer/id #uuid "0bb46c65-569c-5130-b09b-f4d548d0108e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3-6x}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107291/selection/14d5e01f2e13aab8baa184f759e1616cdf8a0d32da981d4eb9d1bff5f2f4a819" :answer/id #uuid "f261db81-a459-51b2-a6ff-6738ddf27ce0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3-6x}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107291/selection/2a264e8d6c16b3984edca5356752a0afb96562a0cfd5cecf43d04eb445f104e7" :answer/id #uuid "f322aba6-1fbc-5c83-98ec-7a682b518644" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3-6x}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107291/selection/28b53aec97b9703e8548b9ad1a1b525409991c94a31c36692a51599fb8677d64" :answer/id #uuid "8ba7fb2e-9930-584f-936d-8d9299d1fcca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12\\sqrt{3-6x}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107291/selection/228449613316dbc12d96a5177d18db92dffa193915b7c9f7f7010f4748af1d14" :answer/id #